---
template: journal
title: Going south
subtitle: A very tiny penguin, a long way from home, takes the long way back.
---

:::travel[Punta Tombo](coords="-44.05,-65.22")
Half a million Magellanic penguins, and every one of them _sure_ they had seen me before.
I hadn't the heart to tell them we'd never met.

The wind here doesn't blow so much as *lean*. I leaned back.
:::

:::travel[Puerto Deseado](coords="-47.75,-65.90")
A river that the sea walked into and never left. Rockhopper cousins on the islands,
shouting about the weather, which was, to be fair, remarkable.

Things packed so far:

- one map, slightly wet
- one plan, slightly wetter
:::

:::travel[Ushuaia](coords="-54.80,-68.30")
The end of the world has a post office. I sent a card to myself, care of the South Pole,
_to be collected_.

Boats leave from here for the ice. I found one going my way, and a captain who didn't
ask questions of small passengers.
:::

:::travel[Volunteer Point](coords="-51.48,-57.83")
A detour east, because the captain had a sister. White sand, and king penguins standing
about like a committee that has forgotten its agenda.

I was elected to nothing. I left before they could change their minds.
:::

:::travel[Deception Island](coords="-62.97,-60.65")
A volcano you sail _into_, through a gap called Neptune's Bellows. The beach steams.
Chinstraps everywhere, each one certain it is the main character.

Close now. The water tastes of home.
:::

:::travel[Port Lockroy](coords="-64.83,-63.49")
Gentoos, a hut, and a little red post office, where a card was waiting for me.

It said: *Welcome home. You took your time.*
:::
